ION.md:67:| P6 (independent), P2 (independent), P0 (recovered); instance premise d | By P6 a record is no assessment or acceptance unless the law requires one, by P2 a step with no route to the outcome is unjustified, and by P0 the record must outlive the actor, so where the applicable law requires no assessment and reserves no acceptance, the grant holder may record the conditions it found satisfied in the existing result surface without adding ceremony, because a step with no route to the outcome is unjustified; the record is no disposition and waives no condition that applies | [Roles and delegation](#roles-and-delegation), Recording a result without review | which conditions require assessment or reserve acceptance: the applicable law and the governing grant; the carrier: [TICKETS](TICKETS.md) | 9, 1 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:76:| P5 (derived from P0 and P6, with P0's open-world premise), P2 (independent), P6 (independent); instance premises a, b | By P5 a step reports only what its context decides, by P2 continuing work needs a route to the destination, and by P6 completion is a claim on evidence against the destination, so preservation, progress, termination and outcome satisfaction are distinct claims, each with its own support, and an exhausted limit or an unresolved attempt proves neither completion nor impossibility | [Construction relation](#construction-relation), Preservation, progress and completion, and Evaluation and completion; [§3](#3-step-results-and-disposition); [§6](#6-cost-and-proportionality) | the completion condition of ongoing work: the owner of its mandate | 5, 7, 9 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:101:- Row 4, configuration and delegation: [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §16](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#existing-authority-selects-the-configuration), [§17](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#17-actor-binding-and-independence), [The executive confi