{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-installation-w8g_16zt/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 268ab114c1b60b31dcd241986d0f15595d1f61c59be1be05e82bb62d6ad9a305 --principal host call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"greeting-acquire-10-1\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/frames/bootstrap.md\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"cbf4a10e8d0b4ca2ab4a1f3ee28a85ffedc3298a0fba666949d9b091e82cc714\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1,53]}},\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:89409a0f1b33367fcea35b9fe1be9f7db4ef05aa37611f453e20a63213645e54\",\"sha256\":\"89409a0f1b33367fcea35b9fe1be9f7db4ef05aa37611f453e20a63213645e54\"},\"id\":\"greeting-acquire-10-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=3ee58b4906194d6eda88b8c1b2b77b34d19118a478f301643e6460fcd5b9958d]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Reference frame bootstrap\\n\\nTask: Enter this method for a task not yet specified: say what the method is, bind the exact basis and the one applicable product definition, say how a reference frame is activated for a step and what the step may and may not do before its contract is admitted, give the core result values, and acquire the deciding owner sections for the task.\\n\\nPurpose: The owning sections for the method's canonical statement; the product lineage objects; the product definition's required relations, recursive discovery and the one constitutional surface with its staleness binding; the authority kinds, the frame tuple and the activation packet; the step's intake and admission; context construction with the size measurement, acquisition, activation and evaluation; and the core result algebra.\\n\\nBinds:\\n\\n- This task binds the construction relation: A is the exact subject and basis the activation binds, Z is the task's required outcome with the acceptance conditions the task states, and the actor's claims keep preservation, progress and outcome satisfaction distinct; a judgment its evidence cannot decide is `indeterminate`, and work it cannot finish is reported as unresolved work, not as a judgment ([../ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation](../ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation); member sha256=56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d; section sha256=6b6c2ce91c5a7e4be765af2f8009252fa8918719e1d885af6b5810ba4eb699da)\\n\\nA `Binds:` item names an obligation the activation of this frame binds, with\\na link to the owning section, the digest of its member and the digest of that\\nsection, or of the span of sections it names, where it names one; the item\\ncopies no section and owns no determination, and where no route of this frame\\ncarries the section the item is a paraphrase of it.\\n\\nEach excerpt below copies one owning section of a member of this method\\nbyte for byte, except a `rows=k/n` excerpt (see below) and except that\\neach relative link destination is rebased\\nto resolve from this directory to the same target. Fenced code, inline\\ncode and absolute and `stdo://` links are unchanged. The `Source:` line\\nbefore an excerpt names the member and the section's anchor, and gives\\nthe SHA-256 of the whole owning member. The section digest recorded in\\nFRAME_INPUTS.json is over the owner's bytes, not over this copy. The\\nowning section decides; this frame owns no determination. An excerpt\\nwhose `Source:` line says `rows=k/n` is a family table of which only\\nthe k rows that cite a section this frame carries are copied, with the\\ntable's preamble, header and every non-family table; the other rows\\nstay in the owning member and are not copied. The frame's\\nqualification, not this selection, decides whether the frame is\\nsufficient for its task.\\n\\nRoutes, in order:\\n\\n1. [SPEC_METHOD.md#canonical-statement](../SPEC_METHOD.md#canonical-statement)\\n2. [FOUNDATIONS.md#product-lineage-objects](../FOUNDATIONS.md#product-lineage-objects)\\n3. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#2-required-definition-relations](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#2-required-definition-relations)\\n4. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#9-recursive-discovery-and-explicit-composition](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#9-recursive-discovery-and-explicit-composition)\\n5. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#11-one-constitutional-surface-and-version-boundary](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#11-one-constitutional-surface-and-version-boundary)\\n6. [FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds](../FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)\\n7. [FOUNDATIONS.md#the-frame-tuple](../FOUNDATIONS.md#the-frame-tuple)\\n8. [REFERENCE_FRAME.md#11-the-activation-packet](../REFERENCE_FRAME.md#11-the-activation-packet)\\n9. [ACTIVATION.md#intake](../ACTIVATION.md#intake)\\n10. [ACTIVATION.md#admission](../ACTIVATION.md#admission)\\n11. [ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope](../ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope)\\n12. [FOUNDATIONS.md#results](../FOUNDATIONS.md#results)\\n13. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#foundation-to-law-binding-a-project-to-the-method](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#foundation-to-law-binding-a-project-to-the-method)\\n14. [REFERENCE_FRAME.md#foundation-to-law](../REFERENCE_FRAME.md#foundation-to-law)\\n15. [SPEC_METHOD.md#foundation-to-law-chain-outcome-and-build-tenant-binding](../SPEC_METHOD.md#foundation-to-law-chain-outcome-and-build-tenant-binding)\\n\\nSize of this frame: 84475 bytes.\\n\\nSource: SPEC_METHOD.md#canonical-statement sha256=b2773dc0c9feb429b6b357bcfd60e7df46e54db8adcb04dc8d6dbfa023b73677\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,53]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"cbf4a10e8d0b4ca2ab4a1f3ee28a85ffedc3298a0fba666949d9b091e82cc714\",\"selected_sha256\":\"0c4be6566c742a6c948e0bc03e7a0607f5b2aed30bfceb3e1b8ba037b552b049\",\"size_bytes\":4463,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/frames/bootstrap.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,53]},\"sha256\":\"cbf4a10e8d0b4ca2ab4a1f3ee28a85ffedc3298a0fba666949d9b091e82cc714\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-installation-w8g_16zt/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 268ab114c1b60b31dcd241986d0f15595d1f61c59be1be05e82bb62d6ad9a305 --principal host call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"greeting-acquire-11-1\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1004,1055]}},\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:b26ae4c2b337704dcb8b43bc4c7d5d16a492ca5f49b07324ab78cd90df2b05d0\",\"sha256\":\"b26ae4c2b337704dcb8b43bc4c7d5d16a492ca5f49b07324ab78cd90df2b05d0\"},\"id\":\"greeting-acquire-11-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=09d6b5c5972c3c370814ee09df75d09427a074e9b0955fb6f08c01e68ad3b2dd]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"A step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\\nexists (P5, P6):\\n\\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\\n\\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\\n\\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\\n\\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \\\"a candidate is available\\\", never\\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (§5) carries it as a\\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\\n(P5, P6).\\n\\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\\n(P6).\\n\\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Refinements). A stop\\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\\nP3).\\n\\n### Disposition\\n\\nThe decision owner disposes an assessed candidate with one of four\\nsemantic dispositions (§1, Roles and delegation; P6, P5). An assessor may recommend one; the\\nrecommendation is evidence for the decision owner, never a disposition\\n([EVALUATION §4](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results)). The disposition is the\\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1004,1055]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"503cf7de07bd21bd57279b2e6bae3b29db70ad3cc24a169474656475c39cefd8\",\"size_bytes\":3256,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1004,1055]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-installation-w8g_16zt/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 268ab114c1b60b31dcd241986d0f15595d1f61c59be1be05e82bb62d6ad9a305 --principal host call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"greeting-acquire-12-1\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1750,1768]}},\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:4a444cf84a870dae2c3eee72dc94de99c59fee6429f8bf7f415dd264939b05e5\",\"sha256\":\"4a444cf84a870dae2c3eee72dc94de99c59fee6429f8bf7f415dd264939b05e5\"},\"id\":\"greeting-acquire-12-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=806d089e4dc2edf7f0fc58d6f02a919ffddb1a6263b107bc46bfbbc205584226]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Transition evidence\\n\\nA reviewable transition identifies the exact candidate, the affected\\nrelations, the changed realisation paths, the authority paths added or\\nremoved, the retained and open seams, the focused proof, any required\\nintegration proof, the explicit non-changes, and, where an assessor was\\nactivated, the assessor's recommended disposition, with the decision\\nowner's disposition beside it once one is made (§3). Consumers\\nchoose the representation. Transition evidence is a read\\nmodel; it does not become specification, design or admission authority\\n(P6, P4b).\\n\\nConstruction uses the cheapest focused proof capable of falsifying the\\nactive relation. Expensive whole-candidate qualification occurs at a\\ndeclared candidate boundary rather than after every local edit, unless the\\naffected risk makes whole-candidate proof necessary (§6). A durable or\\nreconstructable authority claim is not established solely by a same-process\\nproof when loss of incidental process state is a material counterexample:\\nthe proof destroys or excludes the incidental authority and compares the\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1750,1768]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"08d23dd3949b21b80e23fa46bffedff55bfa456a51e1afd8df831b5f13bbd216\",\"size_bytes\":1090,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1750,1768]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
